Reasoning

Entity inventory. The ACLED schema describes conflict events. Distinct real-world entities I can identify:

1. Event — identified by `event_id_cnty` (e.g. `POL1001`). Maps to bsm:Action, whose description explicitly covers "conflict events, incidents, movements". Confidence 0.9, basis description.
2. Actor 1 — identified by `actor1`; class bsm:Actor ("a person or a group of persons able to perform actions"), values like "Military Forces of Poland" / "Unidentified Armed Group". Confidence 0.85, basis description.
3. Actor 2 — same reasoning on `actor2`.
4. Associated actors — `assoc_actor_1` / `assoc_actor_2` name distinct organizations ("Naval Command of Poland"), so they are their own bsm:Actor entities, not literal attributes. The only object property on BattlespaceConcept that can link two actor concepts is bsm:partOf, so I use partOf with moderate confidence (0.45) — explicitly noting the alternative bsm:alternateName was rejected because the associated actor is a distinct entity, not merely an alias. Since they are only defined inline as the target of partOf, their conceptName is carried in the nested property_mappings.
5. Action effect (fatalities) — `fatalities` is exactly the ActionEffect semantics ("effectiveness of an Action … fatalities, casualties, damage"). Fabricated per event: subject expression `effect_{event_id_cnty}`, linked from the event via bsm:hasResult. effectDescriptionCode is a constant "Fatalities"; effectQuantityNumber takes the `fatalities` column. Confidence 0.85/0.9.
6. Event location — `location` name + `latitude`/`longitude`. Class bsm:Location with bsm:locationName, subject expression `loc_{latitude}_{longitude}`; linked via bsm:hasGeographicLocation (declared on BattlespaceConcept, which Action inherits). 
7. Geometry — the lat/lon pair forms a bsm:AbsolutePoint with bsm:latitudeDecimal/bsm:longitudeDecimal (WGS-84 matches the property descriptions). Subject expression `point_{latitude}_{longitude}`; linked from Location via bsm:hasGeometry. Confidence 0.95.
8. Administrative hierarchy — `admin1/admin2/country/region` columns support a chain of bsm:Location entities joined by bsm:partOf (its description literally says it was added for "City, Region, Country" hierarchy). Chains: precise location partOf admin2 partOf admin1 partOf country partOf region, each Location carrying bsm:locationName from its own column. `admin3` is left unmapped — it is empty in all records and its position (finer than `location`) is uncertain; guessing the chain position against an always-empty column would be over-modeling.

Property qualifier decisions. `event_date` could match either bsm:eventStartDateTime or bsm:eventEndDateTime — near-synonyms differing only by start/end. The column is a single occurrence date, so the conventional reading is a start time; I map to eventStartDateTime at 0.72 and treat it as mildly ambiguous. `event_type`/`sub_event_type` ("Battles"/"Armed clash") have one candidate, bsm:classificationCode, but that property is a security classification of the Action, not an event category — the qualifier mismatch makes it ambiguous, so both go unmapped rather than guessed. `interaction` concatenates inter1/inter2 and stays unmapped. `iso`, `geo_precision`, `time_precision`, `year` (redundant with event_date), `source`, `source_scale`, `timestamp`, `civilian_targeting`, and `population_*` have no ontology counterpart and are unmapped. `tags` maps weakly to bsm:additionalInformationText ("information that does not fit any structured attribute") at 0.35. `notes` maps to bsm:actionDescriptionText at 0.85 by name+description. `inter1` ("State forces") fits bsm:typeName (free-text category strings) at 0.68. `event_id_cnty` also maps to bsm:sourceIdentifier, whose description defines it as the primary key from the originating dataset — high confidence.

IRI cross-check. Every iri value's transformation string is copied character-for-character from the referenced entity's subject_transformation: `actor_{actor1}`, `actor_{actor2}`, `actor_{assoc_actor_1}`, `actor_{assoc_actor_2}`, `effect_{event_id_cnty}`, `loc_{latitude}_{longitude}`, `point_{latitude}_{longitude}`, `admin2_{country}_{admin1}_{admin2}`, `admin1_{country}_{admin1}`, `country_{country}`, `region_{region}`. No empty transformation keys are emitted; associations carry nested type_mappings, with nested conceptName property_mappings only where the referenced entity has no standalone subject_mapping (the associated actors).

